  choices = $EXPL$["A flat 21% rate applied uniformly to all accumulated earnings regardless of asset composition","A split rate of 15.5% on cash and cash-equivalent positions and 8% on illiquid non-cash assets","A flat 10% rate applied to all accumulated post-1986 foreign earnings","The pre-TCJA regular corporate rate of 35% applied to all previously deferred earnings"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 965, the TCJA transition tax imposed a one-time repatriation charge on accumulated post-1986 deferred foreign earnings. Cash and cash-equivalent positions were taxed at 15.5%, while illiquid non-cash assets were taxed at 8%. Taxpayers could elect to pay in installments over eight years under Section 965(h).
Wrong (A): The 21% rate is the ongoing corporate income tax rate under the TCJA, not the transition tax rate.
Wrong (C): The 10% rate relates to the deemed tangible income return under GILTI (Section 951A), not the transition tax.
