-- Q983: Owner-Entity Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The shareholder receives proceeds of at least $10,000 from the redemption transaction","The redemption is substantially disproportionate, a complete termination, or not essentially equivalent to a dividend","The redeeming corporation has no accumulated or current earnings and profits","The shareholder held the redeemed stock for more than one year before the redemption"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 302(b), a stock redemption is treated as a sale or exchange rather than a dividend if it meets one of four tests: (1) not essentially equivalent to a dividend, (2) substantially disproportionate, (3) complete termination of interest, or (4) partial liquidation for noncorporate shareholders.
Wrong (A): There is no minimum dollar threshold in Section 302 — the tests focus on ownership changes, not payment amounts.
Wrong (C): E&P status determines dividend treatment for distributions generally, but Section 302(b) tests govern redemption classification regardless of E&P.
Wrong (D): The holding period of the stock is irrelevant to Section 302(b) qualification; it affects only the character of resulting capital gain.$EXPL$
