-- Q993: Owner-Entity Transactions [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["$35,000 is a tax-free return of basis and $15,000 is treated as capital gain","The entire $50,000 is treated as dividend income taxable at ordinary rates","The entire $50,000 is received tax-free as a return of S corporation earnings","$15,000 is taxable as ordinary income and $35,000 reduces stock basis"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 1368(b), distributions from an S corporation with no accumulated E&P are tax-free to the extent of stock basis. The first $35,000 reduces basis to zero as a nontaxable return of capital. The excess $15,000 is treated as gain from sale or exchange of stock under Section 1368(b)(2), taxed as capital gain.
Wrong (B): S corporation distributions with no accumulated E&P are not treated as dividends — the Section 1368(b) ordering rules apply.
Wrong (C): Only the portion up to basis ($35,000) is tax-free; the $15,000 excess is taxable as capital gain.
