  choices = $EXPL$["Three separate trusts are optimal because each trust claims its own distribution deduction, passing income to beneficiaries at individual rates while preserving asset protection","A single trust is best because it consolidates administrative costs and the $600,000 is taxed once at the trust level regardless of distribution","Direct distribution to the children is always preferable because it avoids trust-level taxation and the children''s lower brackets minimize total tax","Three separate trusts provide no benefit because the IRS treats related trusts as a single taxpayer under the grantor trust consolidation rules"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 661, each trust claims a distribution deduction when it distributes income to its beneficiary, shifting taxation to the beneficiary''s individual rates. Three trusts distributing $200,000 each avoid the compressed trust brackets (37% begins at $15,200) and provide asset protection that direct distribution does not offer.
