-- Q1017: Trusts and Estates [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Investment advisory fees paid for managing the trust''s portfolio assets","Tax preparation fees incurred for filing the fiduciary income tax return","Costs that would not have been incurred if the property were not held in trust","Accounting fees for preparing the grantor''s personal income tax returns"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 67(e) and the Supreme Court''s Knight v. Commissioner decision, costs that would not have been incurred if the property were not held in trust — such as trustee fees and trust-specific administration — are fully deductible above the line and exempt from the 2% floor.
